The displays' logical geometry on Wayland (Task 24 of docs/plans/20261014-gpui-frontend.md, GPUI patch 4): GPUI sized
each display as its current mode over the integer `wl_output.scale`, so an output at a fractional scale (an eDP panel
at 1.75 reads 1440x900 instead of its logical 1645x1028) or a rotated one reports bounds the compositor does not lay
surfaces out in, and a layer-shell panel centered against them lands off center. The Wayland client binds
`zxdg_output_manager_v1` (versions 1 to 3) where the compositor has it and asks every output for its xdg-output: its
logical position and size complete the output (with the output's own `done`, or xdg-output's `done` before version
3), and `PlatformDisplay::bounds` of `cx.displays()` and of a window's display read them, falling back to the old
mode-over-scale bounds where the compositor sends none. Additive; X11 and the other platforms are unchanged.
scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies this to the verified crates.io archive.

